(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[17 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [18 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [19 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [20 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [21 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [22 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [23 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [24 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [25 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [27 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [29 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [30 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [31 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [32 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [33 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [36 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [38 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [39 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [40 21 "// the work due at its death"] [41 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [42 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [44 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [46 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [48 2 "// seq is the record's order of making (queue 253): a collection's trash is finalized in it, as CPython's lists"] [49 2 "// keep their objects in the order they were tracked"] [53 1 "// finSeq numbers the records (finMu)."] [56 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [63 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [66 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (finBarrier's sign of progress)"] [67 26 "// the records goFinalized dropped without queueing work (finRounds' sign of progress, queue 418)"] [68 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [70 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [75 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [76 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [77 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [78 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [84 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [85 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [86 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [87 1 "// can find it dead."] [105 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [106 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [122 1 "// finAddr is o's address for finDeleted when its holder lets it go (0: nothing to check); queue 293: sys.settrace's and"] [123 1 "// sys.setprofile's previous function, the thread's only reference to it, whose __del__ CPython runs as the call"] [124 1 "// drops it (test_sys_settrace's test_reentrancy: a __del__ that sets the trace function)."] [136 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [149 3 "// past the budget: the death waits for the next collection, or (queue 553) for the next operation of the"] [150 3 "// cross-interpreter queues and channels while a subinterpreter is held by handles (xiSettleDeaths)"] [159 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [160 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [161 1 "// finalizers have all run (finBarrier), then the drain."] [187 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [197 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [200 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [203 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [208 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [209 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [218 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [237 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [248 1 "// trackDel tracks o, an instance whose class has a __del__, and with note notes it for the moment at its frame's return"] [249 1 "// (finPendAdd; classInfo's delNote)."] [264 1 "// The moment at a frame's return (the user's decision of 2026-11-22, doc/JOURNAL.md: \"Design: 222\"'s DECISION 1, (b)): an"] [265 1 "// instance whose class has a __del__, made while a frame runs, is noted on its thread with that frame's depth"] [266 1 "// (finPendAdd); when a frame that deep returns, one Go collection asks whether it died with the frame (a temporary of its"] [267 1 "// value stack, a local of its own) and its __del__ runs before the caller goes on (finAtReturn), the moment reference"] [268 1 "// counting gives it when no reference outlives the frame. The gate is the thread's finPendDepth against its depth, one"] [269 1 "// load and a compare at each return, false while nothing is noted. A survivor is noted again at the caller's depth, at"] [270 1 "// most finPendChecks times, then left to the next collection; at most finPendMax notes a thread; the collections' time is"] [271 1 "// the moment at del's (finSpent's budget: a tenth of the elapsed wall time and 50 ms), past it the notes are dropped."] [284 1 "// finPendAdd notes tr's object (address a), just tracked with a __del__'s work, on the running thread at its frame's depth."] [296 1 "// finAtReturn is the check at the return of t's frame at depth t.depth+1 (t.depth the caller's now): Go's collection"] [297 1 "// and the drain, rounds while a dead note's weak references are left to clear (finVerify's), then finPendSettle. Not"] [298 1 "// within a drain (a finalizer's own frames return there; the notes wait for a later return), and the gate shut while it"] [299 1 "// runs (a __del__'s frames return within it)."] [311 2 "// goi's registers keep a returned call's values (dropGen's reason): nanoseconds compiled"] [344 1 "// finPendSettle settles t's notes of the frames deeper than d after a return to depth d: when checked, a dead one (its"] [345 1 "// record gone or its __del__ run) dropped, a survivor noted at depth d until its finPendChecks-th check; unchecked (the"] [346 1 "// budget spent), every such note dropped; finPendDepth recomputed."] [373 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [374 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [375 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [376 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [393 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [420 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [447 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [472 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [485 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [506 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [520 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [531 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [532 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [552 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [553 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [558 33 "// get_warnings_attr imports nothing at shutdown (queue 253)"] [585 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [592 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has run every finalizer"] [593 1 "// it queued (finBarrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [602 1 "// finBarrier is the wait after runtime.GC() (queue 316, \"As built: 316\"): until Go's finalizer goroutine has run every"] [603 1 "// finalizer queued so far, or done holds (done nil: never), at most limit. runtime.GC returns with its sweep finished,"] [604 1 "// so every finalizer of its collection is queued by then; runtime/metrics' counts of the finalizers queued and executed"] [605 1 "// (the executed counted once a block of them has run) are equal once all of them ran. A finalizer that does not return"] [606 1 "// (no run counted for 3 ms) ends the wait as the quiet wait it replaces did (218's: 3 ms without a finalizer run)."] [637 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing and drops no record (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [638 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [639 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [642 1 "// finCollectAt is finCollect, at the interpreter's end when exit (finExitRounds for its rounds)."] [664 1 "// finExitRounds is set by the interpreter's end for its collections' rounds (queue 316, \"As built: 316\"): Py_FinalizeEx's"] [665 1 "// finCollect when gc.callbacks is empty, exitCollect. There a round is skipped when no tracked object can be due"] [666 1 "// (finDueLocked): such a round queues nothing. A dead tracked object without work or weak callbacks only has its record"] [667 1 "// dropped and its plain weak references cleared by its Go finalizer, and the end's next collection does that first,"] [668 1 "// before any Python code of the end runs (it runs in drains, each after a collection). Before a cycle collection"] [669 1 "// (finExitOwe) the skipped round is owed: cyCollect runs it before its probe when it has one to make, since a dead object"] [670 1 "// still under its Go finalizer would hold what it reaches through the probe's collection. gc.collect() keeps every"] [671 1 "// round: a program reads its weak references right after it."] [677 1 "// cyGraphFull is whether cyGraph's last walk passed cyMaxNodes (its nil answer then is not \"nothing to probe\")."] [681 21 "// every round (gc.collect, and an end with gc.callbacks)"] [682 21 "// a round no tracked object can be due at skipped"] [683 21 "// skipped and owed to the cycle collection that follows"] [686 1 "// finDueLocked is whether a dead object can be queued at the next collection (finMu held): the queue not empty, or a"] [687 1 "// tracked object with work or weak references with callbacks (exitWorkPending's test, the pending generators left)."] [705 1 "// finMaxRounds bounds finRounds: rounds while each handles something (218's were at most 8). A chain of objects with"] [706 1 "// finalizers, each holding the next (test_ordered_dict's highly nested subclass: 100 of them), is freed by CPython's"] [707 1 "// reference counts at once and by Go's collector a link a collection (Go keeps what a finalizer's object reaches for"] [708 1 "// one more collection), so one gc.collect() takes as many rounds as the chain is long, up to finMaxRounds."] [711 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [712 1 "// ExtFinRounds is finRounds for the lazy packages (queue 550: pysqlite3's commit): the collections and drains that run the"] [713 1 "// finalizers of what is dead now, as CPython's reference counts would have run them already; the number handled."] [718 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [719 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [739 3 "// a round that only dropped records (dead objects with no work: an identity's container, a plain weak"] [740 3 "// reference's referent) handled nothing, but what they held may be dead at the next collection: Go keeps an"] [741 3 "// object with a finalizer, and all it reaches, for one more collection (queue 418: a deep copy's memo, a"] [742 3 "// container id() tracked, then the tuple it held, then the instance with the weak reference)"] [753 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [754 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [771 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [774 59 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [788 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [789 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [790 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [791 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [800 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [801 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [802 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [803 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [804 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [815 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [816 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [817 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [827 1 "// The moment at a call's return (queue 297; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 297\"): CPython's reference counting"] [828 1 "// frees a generator a call leaves suspended when the call drops its last reference (next(gen()), any(gen())): its"] [829 1 "// close then (GeneratorExit thrown in, finally blocks and a monitor's events), its frame's locals with it. pyi knows that"] [830 1 "// moment without a collection when the generator's only holder was the value stack: made by the calling frame's"] [831 1 "// previous instruction (stampGen: the frame's address and instruction, and callSeq, every call counting itself, so no"] [832 1 "// call ran between), not handed out since (f_generator marks it exposed), and the last argument of a consumer that"] [833 1 "// keeps no reference to its arguments (Builtin.dropsArg: next, any, all, min, max, sum, sorted). No instruction ran"] [834 1 "// between its making and the consumer's call, so nothing stored it; the consumer kept nothing; its own frame does not"] [835 1 "// hold it (a frame object does not keep its generator alive in CPython either). dropGen closes it at the return. Cost:"] [836 1 "// an increment per call and a flag test per built-in call; a collection only for its frame's locals with a finalizer"] [837 1 "// due (222's moment, as del's)."] [839 1 "// callSeq counts the calls (callStack, AotCallV, AotCallMethodV; queue 297)."] [842 1 "// stampGen stamps o, a generator just made by f's running instruction, with its making."] [849 1 "// freshGen is o when it is a generator not yet run, made by f's previous instruction with no call since (the call at"] [850 1 "// callSeq n0 the next one) and never handed out: held by the value stack alone, and now by the consumer's arguments."] [860 1 "// dropGen is the consumer's return for a fresh generator g: suspended, it dies now (_PyGen_Finalize: close, its error"] [861 1 "// to sys.unraisablehook), and its frame's locals with a finalizer due are checked at once (222's finDeleted)."] [863 62 "// exposed: f_generator handed out while it ran"] [868 20 "// a frame object handed out before the close (the close's own GeneratorExit traceback is dropped)"] [874 13 "// no frame object held elsewhere: its locals cleared, as _PyFrame_ClearExceptCode's"] [881 2 "// their collections held to a tenth of the wall time of their own (genSpent), apart from del's (finSpent)"] [890 1 "// The moment at a for loop's end (queue 339; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 339\"): CPython frees the generator a"] [891 1 "// for loop iterates when the loop drops it (POP_ITER at a break or a return, the exception's unwinding, the frame's clear)"] [892 1 "// if the loop held the last reference: `for x in gen(): break`. pyi knows it as 297 knows next(gen())'s: a generator"] [893 1 "// stamped by its making frame's call (stampGen), not run, never handed out, whose get-iter is that frame's next"] [894 1 "// instruction and is followed by the loop's for-iter, was held by the value stack alone and now by the loop's iterator"] [895 1 "// slot, which no Python code reaches; holdLoopGen marks it, and the pop that leaves the loop (step's pop, AotDrop, a"] [896 1 "// handler's or the frame's unwinding) closes it there (dropGen: close, its locals at 222's moment). A loop that runs it"] [897 1 "// to its end pops it finished. Cost: none until a loop holds one (loopHeldN), then a check per pop."] [899 1 "// loopHeldN counts the generators held as fresh by their for loops (holdLoopGen): 0, the pops check nothing."] [902 1 "// holdLoopGen is the get-iter of g, a generator not yet run, by the running frame: marked held by its for loop when that"] [903 1 "// frame's previous instruction made it with no call since (stampGen) and the next one is the loop's for-iter."] [917 1 "// loopNext is whether instruction pc of c is a for loop's for-iter, or an inlined comprehension's start that reaches its"] [918 1 "// for-iter with only its own slots' moves between (PEP 709: the shadowed locals saved, the result made, the iterator"] [919 1 "// swapped above them)."] [933 1 "// unhold is g no longer held by its for loop (popped, or finished)."] [941 1 "// dropLoopGen is v popped from f's value stack: a generator f's for loop held, closed now (dropGen)."] [951 1 "// dropLoopGens is f left by an exception (its clear, _PyFrame_ClearLocals: the stack from its bottom): the generators its"] [952 1 "// for loops held closed."] [961 1 "// genSpent is dropGen's collections' time (its locals' checks), held as finSpent is, apart from it."] [964 1 "// scrubSlots is n nested calls, each a window of 16 interface slots that goi clears at a call's entry: under stage 0's"] [965 1 "// goi a returned call's slots above the stack's top keep their values (the checkout's goi clears them since c9047d52),"] [966 1 "// here the closed frame's locals; compiled, nanoseconds."] [976 1 "// genLocalsDue are the addresses of the tracked objects with work or weak references due that f's fast locals and"] [977 1 "// cells hold (at most 4), read before f is dropped."] [1006 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [1033 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [1034 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [1035 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [1036 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [1037 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [1038 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [1039 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [1042 22 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [1043 2 "// gcDebugUncollectable is gc.DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE (the shutdown's garbage list printed, queue 253)"] [1045 33 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [1049 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [1050 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [1051 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [1052 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [1053 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [1054 35 "// gc.garbage"] [1055 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [1059 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [1063 18 "// its record when tracked"] [1064 18 "// its slots that hold a node, by address: a slot in the node itself (a FutureIter's) must not hold it"] [1065 18 "// in step: the slot is a typed pointer (*Dict, *Cell ...), else an Object"] [1066 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [1073 1 "// cyLeaves are the objects a collection's graph does not walk (queue 241): the dictionaries of the modules sys.modules"] [1074 1 "// holds and the builtins' (held from outside: walking them would walk the whole program), and the frames running on a"] [1075 1 "// thread's stack (their slots change under the loop; their Go frames hold them). Set by cyCollect, nil otherwise."] [1078 1 "// cySetLeaves computes cyLeaves for this collection."] [1103 6 "// the classes the module holds under a name (queue 241's plan: such a class a leaf)"] [1128 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an object whose references cyTraverse lists (CPython's tp_traverse), not a leaf of"] [1129 1 "// this collection (cyLeaves), and able to take a probe's Go finalizer (a list's, a dictionary's or a cell's Go finalizer"] [1130 1 "// may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then none of them)."] [1136 90 "// _io's (queue 545)"] [1145 3 "// a frame a Python object may hold (a traceback's, f_back's, gi_frame's), not running on a thread's stack,"] [1146 3 "// not of a generator (the generator's slots fold it in: 222's rule)"] [1153 3 "// a class statement's class (py-odict-1125): its registries hooked by cyHideTypes; a class a module holds under"] [1154 3 "// a name is a leaf (cySetLeaves)"] [1166 1 "// cyWalkable is a generator whose frame's slots can be hidden (queue 224): suspended, with no pointer from its frame"] [1167 1 "// back at it (a generator that reaches itself never has a probe run), and its frame not handed out: what else holds"] [1168 1 "// an escaped frame is not in the graph."] [1173 1 "// cyAllRefs makes cyTraverse list every object a slot holds, not only nodes (the shutdown's walk, exitRefs: queue 253)."] [1178 1 "// cyForced are the dictionaries an exit collection gives as dead (queue 253, pylifecycle.go): seeds of the graph,"] [1179 1 "// probed, never held, an edge into one reaching nothing; cyForcedSeeds the same as objects; cyWeakAlive, when set,"] [1180 1 "// tells whether a weak reference to the trash is outside it (its callback called)."] [1187 1 "// cyVisit is cyTraverse's visitor: a slot of the node, its kind (typed: a pointer of a concrete type, else an Object)"] [1188 1 "// and the node it holds."] [1191 1 "// cyTraverse is tp_traverse (queue 241; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 241\"): f called with each slot of o (a"] [1192 1 "// node) that holds a node. Only slots o owns alone are listed: a backing array shared with another holder would hide"] [1193 1 "// that holder's reference. A reference the table does not list (a map's, a closure's, a field of a struct that is no"] [1194 1 "// object) stays visible to Go's collector, which only keeps more alive."] [1263 2 "// ioDictP is an _io object's dict (iobase's tp_dictoffset), walked as an instance's (queue 545)"] [1278 20 "// handed out as an object: a node of its own (queue 241)"] [1285 31 "// _asyncio's Future or Task: the slots of a task's cycle (queue 224)"] [1419 3 "// a class (py-odict-1125): its namespace, bases, MRO (itself first) and metaclass; its caches are dropped by"] [1420 3 "// cyHideTypes before a probe"] [1452 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [1500 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [1501 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1594 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1595 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1596 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers have all run (finBarrier); then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1597 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1617 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1707 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1708 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1709 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1710 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1744 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1755 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1